 "name": "mpe",
 "title": "MPE for Peak",
 "version": "0.8",
 "label": "MPE8 Ver 108.469",
 "summary": "Per-note pitch bend, pressure (channel or poly aftertouch) and slide (MPE) on the Peak's 8 voices, a per-patch MPE switch (VOICE page) and Settings MPE pages; one or two zones. v0.2: the arpeggiator ignores its own notes when a DAW sends them back (MIDI loop). v0.3: turning a knob shows envelope times in ms and the filter cutoff in Hz, with a value bar, and Pickup shows an arrow and a distance bar. v0.4: Settings > MPE > PressCurve chooses stock's squared pressure or a linear curve. v0.5: CC 11 on a member channel works as pressure. v0.6: Settings > MPE EXTRAS > EnvSync sets the amp Decay and Release to a note length (1/2 to 1/16) at the current tempo (v0.7: a changed setting applies after 1 s). v0.8: hold Mod and move a slider or knob to put its modulation destination in the first free matrix slot; the encoder chooses the source. Tested on one Peak with the automated hardware test rig and played from a LinnStrument.",
 "built": {
  "commit": "4ac5d918500a",
  "definition": "patches/peak_mpe/patch.py"
 },
